<h2>Common cosmetic options</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><a href="/services/teeth-whitening/">Professional teeth whitening</a> — significantly stronger and longer-lasting than over-the-counter strips.</li>
  <li><a href="/services/veneers/">Porcelain veneers</a> — thin, hand-shaped porcelain shells bonded to the front of teeth.</li>
  <li><a href="/services/clear-aligners/">Clear aligners</a> — straighten crooked or shifted teeth without metal braces.</li>
  <li>Tooth-colored fillings and bonding — repair small chips, gaps, or worn edges.</li>
  <li><a href="/services/crowns-bridges/">Crown replacements</a> — modern all-ceramic crowns where old metal ones used to be.</li>
  <li>Full smile makeovers — combining several procedures into a single coordinated plan.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which option fits what's bothering you?</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li><strong>Yellowed or dull teeth:</strong> start with <a href="/services/teeth-whitening/">professional whitening</a>. If staining is deep or uneven and doesn't respond, veneers or bonding can cover it.</li>
  <li><strong>A small chip or gap:</strong> tooth-colored bonding is often a single, affordable visit.</li>
  <li><strong>Crooked, crowded or shifted teeth:</strong> <a href="/services/clear-aligners/">clear aligners</a> move the teeth themselves, so less tooth needs to be reshaped later.</li>
  <li><strong>Worn, short or uneven front teeth:</strong> <a href="/services/veneers/">porcelain veneers</a> change shape, length and color at once.</li>
  <li><strong>Old dark crowns or missing teeth:</strong> new all-ceramic crowns, bridges or <a href="/services/dental-implants/">dental implants</a> restore the look and the bite.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we plan cosmetic work</h2>
<p>Every cosmetic case starts with a real conversation about what bothers you and what you'd like the outcome to look like. We use digital imaging and try-in mockups so you can see and approve the plan before any final work is done. We won't talk you into veneers if a simpler option will get the job done.</p>
<p>Healthy gums and teeth come first. If there's decay, gum inflammation, or a bite problem that would shorten the life of cosmetic work, we'll address it before — or as part of — the cosmetic plan, so your investment lasts.</p>

<h2>How long does it take?</h2>
<p>Whitening can be done in one visit. Veneers and crowns generally take two visits over a few weeks. Clear aligner cases typically run 6 to 18 months depending on the amount of movement. Full makeovers are usually phased over a few months.</p>

<h2>What cosmetic dentistry costs</h2>
<p>Cost depends on how many teeth are involved and which materials are right for you, so we quote after an exam rather than guessing online. You'll get a written estimate before any treatment, and we'll show you lower-cost alternatives side by side. Ask about Cherry financing and in-house payment plans on our <a href="/insurance-financing/">insurance &amp; financing</a> page, and new patients without insurance can start with our <a href="/special-offers/">$49 new-patient exam and X-rays</a>.</p>

<h2>A cosmetic dentist in Tempe who also does the hard stuff</h2>
<p>Dr. Matthew Phillips places and restores implants, builds dentures and handles extractions in the same office, so a smile makeover that needs more than cosmetic work doesn't mean being sent across town. Learn more <a href="/about/">about Dr. Phillips</a>.</p>

<p>Explore examples in our <a href="/before-after-gallery/">before-and-after gallery</a>. Individual results vary, and your consultation will focus on options appropriate for you.</p>
